# Payroll & Benefits Coordinator
  text: Betterment HQ - New York City
  [button] Apply
# About Betterment
# About the Role
  text: As Payroll & Benefits Coordinator, you will be responsible for supporting on-time payroll processing and effective benefits administration. 
  text: This is a salaried, non-exempt role that is based out of our NYC office. Below we've reflected the base salary range we would offer for this
  text: New York City: $70,000 - $83,000
# A Day in the Life
  text: Prepare semi-monthly payroll for exempt and non-exempt employees, ensuring accuracy and timeliness
  text: Review and reconcile timesheets, PTO balances, and payroll data inputs prior to each pay run
  text: Process payroll adjustments including new hires, terminations, pay changes, garnishments, and voluntary deductions
  text: Support preparation of year-end payroll activities including W-2 distribution and reconciliation
  text: Respond to employee inquiries about pay, deductions, and paycheck reconciliation in a timely and professional manner
  text: Administer employee benefits programs including health, dental, vision, life insurance, 401(k), FSA/HSA, and wellness offerings
  text: Coordinate open enrollment periods — prepare communications, host informational sessions, and guide employees through elections
  text: Process enrollments, qualifying life event changes, and terminations with insurance carriers and benefit platforms
  text: Reconcile monthly benefit invoices and coordinate with Finance to ensure accurate payroll deductions
  text: Serve as a first point of contact for employee questions about coverage, eligibility, and claims
  text: Compliance & Recordkeeping
  text: Maintain accurate and confidential employee records in the HRIS and payroll system
  text: Assist with compliance filings and reporting, including ACA, COBRA, ERISA, and state/local requirements
